# CONTEXT.md

Architecture map, domain glossary, and codebase conventions.
Read by Claude Code agents before grilling, architecture proposals, or refactor sessions — so they anchor suggestions in the team's shared vocabulary.

**How to maintain:** Update as understanding evolves. Add terms when they stabilize. ADRs record *why* decisions were made; this file records *what* is true now.

---

## Architecture map

One row per module: a skill, a shared or person agent, or a code module. An agent a skill owns is listed in that skill's Private agents cell and has no row of its own. Link each module's Interface, the one place its contract is written (`rules/modules.md`).

| Module | Kind | Owns | Private agents | Depends on | Interface |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| _Module_ | _skill / agent (shared) / agent (person) / code module_ | _What it owns, in one line_ | _Agents only it uses, or —_ | _Modules it uses, or —_ | _path/to/file.md#interface_ |

